# requirements-dev.in — THE DEV TOOLS A PERSON EDITS (CK-72). The file beside
# it, `requirements-dev.txt`, is GENERATED from this one and is never edited
# by hand. It is constrained to the runtime lock (the -c line below), so the
# suite runs on exactly the tree Render installs plus these tools, and a
# shared package (anyio, idna, h11, typing-extensions) can never sit at one
# version here and another there. Regenerate from backend/ after editing this
# file, and again after any recompile of requirements.txt:
#   uv pip compile requirements-dev.in --universal --python-version 3.13 --generate-hashes -o requirements-dev.txt
# Local install, both locks in one hash-checked pip call:
#   pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
# Nothing here reaches Render: render.yaml installs requirements.txt alone, and
# tests/test_requirements_lock.py pins that the runtime lock names no dev tool.
# Every pin is `==`, at the version the local venv ran on 2026-10-11: the dev
# tools were never deployed, so the versions the suite passed on are the
# verified ones.
-c requirements.txt
pytest==9.1.1
pytest-asyncio==1.4.0
httpx==0.28.1
# uv (CK-72) — the universal resolver that compiles both locks. A DEV tool
# only: it is never in requirements.txt and never on Render.
uv==0.13.0
